  "choices": [
    {
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "index": 0,
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"question_material\": [\n    {\n      \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n      \"examples\": [\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Nomura et al., 2020\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供SCFAs在实体瘤抗PD-1治疗中促进疗效的临床关联证据。\",\n          \"finding\": \"在52名接受抗PD-1免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的实体瘤患者中，粪便中乙酸、丙酸、丁酸和戊酸的增加与更好的无进展生存期（PFS）相关（HR分别为0.29, 0.08, 0.31, 0.53）。血清异戊酸水平升高也与更好的预后相关（HR 0.38）。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为52名接受抗PD-1 ICI治疗的实体瘤患者；测量指标为粪便中的短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）及血清异戊酸水平。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R81\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Botticelli et al., 2020\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供SCFAs在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）抗PD-1治疗中促进疗效的临床关联证据。\",\n          \"finding\": \"在接受抗PD-1治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者中，粪便中丙酸水平的显著升高与治疗响应者相关。血清代谢组学分析显示，乙酸、丁酸和丙酸的浓度与抗PD-1治疗的响应呈正相关，且与CD8+ T细胞上的PD-1表达呈正相关。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为11名接受纳武利尤单抗（anti-PD-1）治疗的NSCLC患者；比较对象为治疗响应者与无响应者。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R82\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Kang et al., 2023\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供丁酸通过特定机制增强抗PD-1疗效的机制研究案例。\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道菌Roseburia intestinalis产生的丁酸通过激活细胞毒性CD8+ T细胞，增强了结直肠癌（CRC）模型中抗PD-1疗法的疗效。具体表现为增加了CD8+ T细胞的浸润和活化，抑制了微卫星不稳定性高（MSI-high）CRC的肿瘤生长，并在微卫星稳定（MSS）CRC中与抗PD-1疗法协同作用以克服耐药性。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为小鼠结直肠癌（CRC）模型；干预措施为补充丁酸或定植产丁酸菌；靶点为抗PD-1疗法。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R84\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Coutzac et al., 2020\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供SCFAs对另一种ICI靶点（CTLA-4）产生双向调节作用（此处为抑制/负面效应）的案例。\",\n          \"finding\": \"系统性短链脂肪酸限制了癌症宿主中CTLA-4阻断的抗肿瘤效果。在40名接受抗CTLA-4（伊匹木单抗）治疗的转移性黑色素瘤患者中，血清丁酸和丙酸水平与PFS和总生存期（OS）呈负相关。小鼠模型证实，口服丁酸降低了抗CTLA-4的疗效，并限制了T细胞上ICOS的上调和肿瘤特异性T细胞的积累。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为40名接受抗CTLA-4治疗的转移性黑色素瘤患者及小鼠模型；比较对象为不同血清SCFA水平；靶点为抗CTLA-4疗法。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R85\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Murayama et al., 2024\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供支链脂肪酸（BCFA）增强抗PD-1疗效的案例。\",\n          \"finding\": \"异丁酸（一种BCFA）增强了抗PD-1抗体在小鼠CT26结肠癌模型中的抗肿瘤效果。这种协同效应伴随着肿瘤内PD-1和IFN-γ水平的升高，以及CD3+ T细胞向肿瘤组织浸润的增加。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为小鼠结肠癌模型；干预措施为口服异丁酸联合抗PD-1抗体。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R86\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Kocher et al., 2021\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供色氨酸衍生物（IDO活性）导致ICI耐药的临床关联证据。\",\n          \"finding\": \"在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者队列中，血浆IDO（吲哚胺2,3-双加氧酶）活性升高与原发性免疫治疗耐药相关。进展性疾病患者的IDO活性在治疗后显著增加，而治疗响应者的IDO活性保持稳定。进展患者还表现出较高的血浆色氨酸水平。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为23名接受抗PD-1治疗的NSCLC患者；测量指标为治疗前后的血浆IDO活性和色氨酸水平。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R87\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Renga et al., 2022\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供色氨酸衍生物（ICA）增强抗PD-L1疗效的机制研究案例。\",\n          \"finding\": \"由益生菌Lactobacillus产生的吲哚-3-甲醛（ICA）改善了黑色素瘤小鼠模型的抗肿瘤免疫。口服ICA联合抗PD-L1治疗比单独使用抗PD-L1显著减少了肿瘤生长。机制上，ICA激活AHR通路，刺激CD8+ T细胞产生IFN-γ，从而增强ICI的有效性。富含色氨酸的饮食作为前体放大了这一效果。在42名接受抗PD-1和IFN-α治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，血清基线ICA水平在响应者中显著更高。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象包括黑色素瘤小鼠模型和42名黑色素瘤患者；干预措施为ICA补充或高色氨酸饮食；靶点为抗PD-L1/PD-1疗法。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R89\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Fong et al., 2023\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供色氨酸衍生物（I-3-CA）通过竞争性结合AHR增强抗PD-1疗效的机制研究案例。\",\n          \"finding\": \"由益生菌Lactobacillus gallinarum分泌的色氨酸衍生物吲哚-3-羧酸（I-3-CA）增强了微卫星不稳定（MC38）和稳定（CT26）结直肠癌小鼠模型中对抗PD-1疗法的反应。I-3-CA与犬尿氨酸竞争结合AHR。在CD4+ T细胞中，I-3-CA抵消了犬尿氨酸诱导的AHR激活及其向Treg细胞的分化。此外，I-3-CA降低了肿瘤微环境（TME）中IDO1的表达，减少了犬尿氨酸的产生，降低了Treg细胞的浸润，并增强了CD8+ T细胞的功能。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为结直肠癌小鼠模型及患者来源的类器官；机制涉及AHR和IDO1/Kynurenine通路的相互作用。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R26\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Cong et al., 2024\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供胆汁酸（BA）抑制CD8+ T细胞功能并促进肿瘤生长的案例。\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道微生物修饰的胆汁酸（特别是脱氧胆酸DCA）通过抑制Ca2+-NFAT2信号传导来抑制CD8+ T细胞的效应功能。携带DCA生物合成基因的细菌存在与CD8+ T细胞活性降低和肿瘤生长增加相关。这种效应可以通过螯合、基因删除或噬菌体靶向DCA产生菌（Clostridium scindens）来逆转。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为结直肠癌模型；关键代谢物为DCA；机制涉及Ca2+-NFAT2信号通路。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R91\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Lee et al., 2022\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供胆汁酸（UDCA）与肝细胞癌（HCC）抗PD-1治疗响应相关的临床关联证据。\",\n          \"finding\": \"在接受ICI治疗的不可切除肝细胞癌（HCC）患者中，响应者粪便样本中富集了熊去氧胆酸（UDCA）和鹅去氧胆酸。然而，在一项转化研究中，原发性和次级胆汁酸在肝癌样本中积累，高水平的胆汁酸与肿瘤特异性T细胞反应减弱和对抗PD-1疗法的耐药性相关。抑制胆汁酸结合酶增强了免疫疗法疗效。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为接受ICI治疗的HCC患者及肝癌样本；比较对象为不同胆汁酸水平与T细胞反应及治疗响应的关系。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R92\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Varanasi et al., 2025\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接材料：提供胆汁酸合成阻碍肝脏癌症中肿瘤特异性T细胞反应的机制研究。\",\n          \"finding\": \"胆汁酸合成阻碍了肝脏癌症期间的肿瘤特异性T细胞反应。高胆汁酸水平与抗PD-1疗法的耐药性相关。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"研究对象为肝细胞癌模型；关注胆汁酸合成途径对T细胞功能的影响。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R93\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"explanation\": \"微生物代谢物在不同肿瘤类型和免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）靶点下表现出复杂的双向调节作用，其机制主要依赖于特定的受体信号通路和免疫细胞亚群的重编程。\\n\\n1. **短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）的双向调节**：\\n   - **促进机制**：SCFAs（如丁酸、丙酸）通常通过激活G蛋白偶联受体（GPR41, GPR43, GPR109A）和作为组蛋白去乙酰化酶（HDAC）抑制剂发挥作用。丁酸通过HDAC抑制促进Foxp3启动子区域的组蛋白H3乙酰化，诱导结肠调节性T细胞（Treg）分化，同时通过上调ID2介导的IL-12信号通路增强CD8+ T细胞的效应功能和记忆潜力。在抗PD-1/PD-L1治疗中，SCFAs通过促进抗原呈递和CD8+ T细胞浸润来提高疗效。\\n   - **抑制机制**：在某些情况下，SCFAs可能限制抗肿瘤免疫。例如，在抗CTLA-4治疗中，系统性SCFAs（如丁酸）可能通过扩大Treg细胞群体或限制ICOS的上调来抑制疗效。这表明SCFAs的作用取决于具体的ICI靶点（PD-1 vs CTLA-4）和肿瘤微环境背景。\\n\\n2. **色氨酸衍生物的双向调节**：\\n   - **促炎/抗肿瘤机制**：微生物产生的吲哚类代谢物（如ICA、IPA、I-3-CA）主要作为芳烃受体（AHR）的配体。它们通过AHR信号通路刺激CD8+ T细胞产生IFN-γ，增强抗肿瘤免疫。I-3-CA还能通过与犬尿氨酸竞争结合AHR，拮抗犬尿氨酸诱导的Treg分化，并下调TME中的IDO1表达，从而减少免疫抑制。\\n   - **抗炎/促肿瘤机制**：宿主或微生物产生的犬尿氨酸（Kynurenine）是IDO酶的产物，它通过激活AHR诱导Treg分化和T细胞功能障碍，导致免疫逃逸和ICI耐药。因此，IDO活性升高通常与较差的治疗响应相关。\\n\\n3. **胆汁酸（BAs）的双向调节**：\\n   - **促炎/抗肿瘤机制**：某些初级和次级胆汁酸（如CDCA、LCA）可通过激活TGR5受体增强I型干扰素（IFN-I）的表达，从而增强抗病毒和抗肿瘤免疫。UDCA作为FXR拮抗剂，在某些背景下（如allo-SCT）显示出保护作用。\\n   - **抑制/耐药机制**：微生物修饰的次级胆汁酸（如DCA、LCA）可通过多种机制促进耐药。DCA通过抑制Ca2+-NFAT2信号传导抑制CD8+ T细胞的效应功能。LCA及其衍生物可作为FXR配体，下调回肠血管中MAdCAM-1的表达，促使免疫抑制性Treg17细胞从肠道迁移至肿瘤和淋巴结，从而促进ICI耐药。在肝细胞癌中，高浓度的胆汁酸积累与肿瘤特异性T细胞反应减弱相关。\\n\\n总体而言，代谢物的双向调节作用受限于ICI的类型（PD-1/CTLA-4）、肿瘤的组织学类型（如黑色素瘤、结直肠癌、肝癌）、代谢物的局部与全身分布以及宿主微生物组的组成。\",\n      \"remaining_points\": [\n        \"不同代谢物在具体肿瘤亚型中的剂量依赖性效应尚需更多临床验证。\",\n        \"代谢物组合（如SCFAs与色氨酸衍生物联合）对ICI疗效的协同或拮抗作用机制尚不明确。\",\n        \"胆汁酸受体（FXR/TGR5）在不同免疫细胞亚群中的具体信号转导差异有待进一步解析。\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "Here's a thinking process:\n\n1.  **Understand User Goal:** The user wants me to act as a researcher preparing targeted reading notes for a literature review author. The goal is to extract information-rich, editable research material based on a specific question.\n2.  **Analyze the Prompt Requirements:**\n    *   **Task 1: `examples`**: Extract useful specific studies into independent notes. One note per paper/study. Different authors/papers get separate items. Do not merge two studies sharing subjects/models/conditions. Multiple experiments in one paper can be separate items. `finding` must fully explain what was done, specific findings, methods, mechanisms, or arguments. `conditions` must retain important conditions, comparisons, study settings, and differences linked to results. Quantitative results must keep their metrics and subjects. `use_in_review` must specify its role for the current task (e.g., correlation analysis, causal/mechanism analysis, prediction/model validation, intervention, theoretical/methodological argument). Distinguish between direct answers to the question and background/comparative studies. Keep relevant background but label it clearly.\n    *   **Task 2: `explanation`**: Organize concepts, principles, mechanisms, and the author's own synthesized explanations explicitly stated in the article, serving the asked question. Do not turn `examples` into a mini-review here. Do not create new cross-study summary conclusions. Do not synthesize percentages from different studies into ranges. Do not change identities of objects/materials/data/methods. Do not turn study settings into universal rules. Explanations must be concrete, clear, explaining processes and relationships, avoiding empty topic lists.\n    *   **Other constraints**: Omit method details not explicitly provided. Note unanswered questions briefly in `remaining_points`. Only organize actual information provided, no guessing. Identify original studies as \"本研究\" (if applicable, though this is a review, so I'll use author/year as given). Use Chinese with necessary terms. Output only JSON in the specified structure.\n    *   **Question**: \"提取不同代谢物（SCFAs、色氨酸衍生物、胆汁酸）在不同肿瘤及 ICI 靶点下的双向调节作用的具体案例及受体机制。\" (Extract specific cases and receptor mechanisms of the bidirectional regulatory effects of different metabolites (SCFAs, tryptophan derivatives, bile acids) under different tumors and ICI targets.)\n    *   **Source Material**: A comprehensive review article titled \"Microbiota-derived metabolites: Key modulators of cancer immunotherapies.\" It covers SCFAs, Tryptophan metabolites/Indoles, Bile Acids, and their roles in ICIs, allo-SCT, CAR-T, etc. It contains many cited studies (Nomura et al., Botticelli et al., Kang et al., Coutzac et al., Murayama et al., Kocher et al., Fong et al., Cong et al., Lee et al., Varanasi et al., etc.).\n\n3.  **Deconstruct the Question & Map to Source:**\n    *   *Metabolites*: SCFAs, Tryptophan derivatives (Indoles), Bile Acids.\n    *   *Context*: Different tumors & ICI targets (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, etc.).\n    *   *Key Aspect*: Bidirectional regulatory effects (promote vs. inhibit/suppress efficacy) + Receptor mechanisms.\n    *   *Need to extract*: Specific cases from the text showing how these metabolites have opposite/context-dependent effects depending on tumor type or ICI target, along with the receptors involved.\n\n4.  **Scan Source for Relevant Information (Mental Walkthrough):**\n    *   *SCFAs*:\n        *   Positive effect on anti-PD-1: Nomura et al. (solid tumors, n=52): stool acetic, propionic, butyric, valeric acids associated with better PFS (HRs <1). Mechanism: HDAC inhibition, GPR43 activation -> CD8+ T cell infiltration/activation. Kang et al. (CRC mouse model): Roseburia intestinalis/butyrate boosts anti-PD-1 by activating cytotoxic CD8+ T cells. Murayama et al. (mouse CT26 colon cancer): Isobutyric acid enhances anti-PD-1 efficacy.\n        *   Negative effect on anti-CTLA-4: Coutzac et al. (metastatic melanoma, n=40): serum butyric and propionic acids inversely correlated with PFS/OS. Mouse models: oral butyric acid reduced anti-CTLA-4 efficacy, restrained ICOS upregulation and tumor-specific T cell accumulation. Mechanism: expands T reg cells.\n        *   Bidirectional/Context-dependent explanation in text: \"The seemingly contradictory effects of SCFAs on ICI efficacy... are likely rooted in multiple context-dependent variables. First, the type of ICI targeted is critical: butyric acid may enhance anti-PD-1/PD-L1 efficacy by promoting CD8+ T cell activation yet may impair anti-CTLA-4 responses by expanding T reg cells. Second, tumor type matters... Third, source of measurement (stool vs serum)...\"\n        *   Receptors/Mechanisms: GPR41, GPR43, GPR109A, HDAC inhibition.\n    *   *Tryptophan Derivatives / Indoles*:\n        *   Positive: ICA (indole-3-carboxaldehyde) improves anti-tumor immunity in melanoma mouse model + anti-PD-L1. Activates AHR pathway -> stimulates IFN-γ in CD8+ T cells. Renga et al. (melanoma patients n=42): baseline serum ICA higher in responders. IPA (indole-3-propionic acid) enhances anti-PD-1 in CRC mouse model -> promotes CD8+ T cell differentiation into Tex cells. I-3-CA (indole-3-carboxylic acid) enhances anti-PD-1 in MC38/CT26 CRC models -> competes with kynurenine for AHR binding, reduces IDO1 expression, lowers T reg infiltration.\n        *   Negative/Complex: Kynurenine (tryptophan metabolite via host IDO) is immunosuppressive. High IDO activity linked to primary resistance in NSCLC (Kocher et al., n=23). Patients with progressive disease had increased IDO activity. Tryptophan depletion/kynurenine overload causes T cell dysfunction.\n        *   Bidirectional/Context: Indoles generally promote anti-tumor immunity via AHR, but the IDO/Kynurenine pathway suppresses it. The balance depends on microbial vs host metabolism. Also, ICA protects against ICI-associated colitis without compromising anti-tumor effects.\n        *   Receptors/Mechanisms: AHR (aryl hydrocarbon receptor), IDO1/Kynurenine pathway, IFN-I signaling.\n    *   *Bile Acids (BAs)*:\n        *   Positive: UDCA and ursocholic acid enriched in stool of HCC patients responding to ICIs. Primary/secondary BAs accumulated in liver HCC samples, but high BA levels correlated with reduced tumor-specific T cell responses and resistance to anti-PD-1 (Varanasi et al., Science 2025). Wait, this says high BA = resistance. But another study says UDCA/enriched in responders. Let's check carefully: \"In HCC patients treated with ICIs, ursodeoxycholic acid (UDCA) and ursocholic acid were enriched in the stool samples of responder patients. In a translational study, primary and secondary BAs accumulated in liver HCC samples. High BA levels correlated with reduced tumor-specific T cell responses and resistance to anti-PD-1 therapy...\" This shows context/tissue specificity (stool vs liver/HCC tissue).\n        *   Negative: LCA and derivatives act as FXR ligands, suppress MAdCAM-1 in ileal vasculature -> weakened retention of immunosuppressive T reg17 cells in gut -> migrate to tumors/lymph nodes -> promote ICI resistance. DCA suppresses CD8+ T cell effector function by inhibiting Ca2+-NFAT2 signaling. Presence of DCA-producing bacteria correlates with reduced CD8+ activity and increased tumor growth.\n        *   Bidirectional/Context: \"BAs exhibit dual effects: Some secondary BAs promote ICI resistance by facilitating T reg cell migration, while others enhance anti-tumor immunity. BAs' context-dependent effects may rely on their structural class, site of action, tumor context, and patient-individual factors such as antibiotics or microbial shifts.\"\n        *   Receptors/Mechanisms: FXR (farnesoid X receptor), TGR5, NFAT2 signaling, MAdCAM-1 downregulation.\n\n5.  **Structure the Output according to Instructions:**\n    *   Need to format as JSON: `{\"question_material\": [{\"question_id\": \"Q01\", \"examples\": [...], \"explanation\": \"...\", \"remaining_points\": []}]}`\n    *   For `examples`: Each item needs `attribution`, `use_in_review`, `finding`, `conditions`, `reference_ids`.\n    *   I will group them logically by metabolite class as requested, ensuring each study is separate.\n    *   I need to carefully map the references from the optional_bibliography to the extracted studies.\n    *   Let's draft the examples step-by-step.\n\n    *Example 1: SCFAs - Positive effect on anti-PD-1*\n    - Attribution: Nomura et al. (2020) [R81]\n    - Finding: Stool levels of acetic, propionic, butyric, and valeric acids were positively associated with progression-free survival (PFS) in solid tumor patients receiving anti-PD-1 ICIs. HRs ranged from 0.08 to 0.53. Plasma isovaleric acid also showed positive association.\n    - Conditions: n=52 patients with solid tumors; anti-PD-1 treatment (nivolumab or pembrolizumab); fecal metabolomics measured pre-treatment.\n    - Use_in_review: 关联分析，提供SCFAs水平与抗PD-1疗效正相关的临床证据，用于说明特定ICI靶点下SCFAs的促免疫作用。\n    - Ref: R81\n\n    *Example 2: SCFAs - Negative effect on anti-CTLA-4*\n    - Attribution: Coutzac et al. (2020) [R85]\n    - Finding: Serum levels of butyric and propionic acids were inversely correlated with PFS and OS in metastatic melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab). Preclinical models showed oral butyric acid reduced anti-CTLA-4 efficacy by restraining ICOS upregulation on T cells and limiting tumor-specific T cell accumulation.\n    - Conditions: n=40 patients with metastatic melanoma; anti-CTLA-4 treatment; serum metabolomics; mouse models challenged with tumors.\n    - Use_in_review: 关联分析与机制验证，提供SCFAs在抗CTLA-4治疗中发挥抑制作用的对比案例，支撑双向调节作用的论述。\n    - Ref: R85\n\n    *Example 3: Tryptophan Derivatives - Indoles (ICA/IPA/I-3-CA) enhancing anti-PD-1*\n    - Attribution: Fong et al. (2023) [R26] & Renga et al. (2022) [R89] & Bender et al. (2023) [R58] (I'll combine or pick one main mechanism paper, but instructions say separate papers. I'll stick to Fong et al. for I-3-CA mechanism, and Renga/Bender for clinical/preclinical validation. Actually, I'll make separate entries for clarity.)\n    - Let's do Fong et al. (2023) [R26]: I-3-CA secreted by Lactobacillus gallinarum enhanced anti-PD-1 response in MC38 and CT26 CRC mouse models. Competes with kynurenine for AHR binding in CD4+ T cells, counteracting T reg differentiation. Reduces IDO1 expression in TME, decreasing kynurenine production and T reg infiltration, enhancing CD8+ T cell function.\n    - Conditions: Microsatellite-unstable MC38 and microsatellite-stable CT26 CRC mouse models; anti-PD-1 therapy; in vitro CD4+ T cell treatment.\n    - Use_in_review: 机制分析，阐明色氨酸衍生物（I-3-CA）通过竞争性结合AHR和下调IDO1通路逆转免疫抑制的具体分子机制。\n    - Ref: R26\n\n    *Example 4: Tryptophan Derivatives - Host IDO/Kynurenine pathway suppressing anti-PD-1*\n    - Attribution: Kocher et al. (2021) [R87]\n    - Finding: High plasma indoleamine-2,3-dioxygenase 1 (IDO) activity was significantly linked to primary resistance to immunotherapy in NSCLC patients. Patients with progressive disease showed increased IDO activity and higher plasma tryptophan levels, indicating active tryptophan breakdown leading to T cell dysfunction.\n    - Conditions: n=23 NSCLC patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy; plasma IDO activity and tryptophan levels measured before and at first follow-up.\n    - Use_in_review: 关联分析，提供宿主代谢途径（IDO/犬尿氨酸）导致ICI耐药的反向案例，与微生物色氨酸衍生物的促效作用形成对照，完善双向调节背景。\n    - Ref: R87\n\n    *Example 5: Bile Acids - Context-dependent effects in HCC (Stool vs Tissue)*\n    - Attribution: Lee et al. (2022) [R92] & Varanasi et al. (2025) [R93]\n    - Finding: In HCC patients treated with ICIs, UDCA and ursocholic acid were enriched in stool samples of responders. Conversely, a translational study found that primary and secondary BAs accumulated in liver HCC tissues, where high BA levels correlated with reduced tumor-specific T cell responses and resistance to anti-PD-1 therapy. Inhibiting BA-conjugating enzyme enhanced immunotherapy efficacy.\n    - Conditions: Unresectable HCC patients treated with ICIs; stool metabolomics vs. liver tissue BA quantification; enzyme inhibition in translational models.\n    - Use_in_review: 关联分析与组织特异性比较，展示胆汁酸在不同检测部位（粪便vs肿瘤组织）呈现相反临床结局的案例，强调空间分布对ICI疗效的双向影响。\n    - Ref: R92, R93\n\n    *Example 6: Bile Acids - Secondary BAs promoting ICI resistance via T reg migration & CD8 suppression*\n    - Attribution: Fidelle et al. (2023) [R90] & Cong et al. (2024) [R91]\n    - Finding: Post-antibiotic recolonization by Enterocloster increased secondary BAs like LCA. LCA acts as an FXR ligand, suppressing MAdCAM-1 expression in ileal vasculature, which weakens retention of immunosuppressive T reg17 cells in the gut, allowing them to migrate to tumors and lymph nodes to promote ICI resistance. Separately, elevated DCA in CRC patients suppressed CD8+ T cell effector function by inhibiting Ca2+-NFAT2 signaling via plasma membrane Ca2+ ATPase.\n    - Conditions: Mouse models post-antibiotic dysbiosis; human CRC patients; FXR signaling and NFAT2/Ca2+ pathways investigated.\n    - Use_in_review: 机制分析，提供次级胆汁酸通过FXR-MAdCAM-1轴促进Treg迁移以及通过NFAT2信号抑制CD8+ T细胞功能的具体案例，解释胆汁酸介导ICI耐药的负面调节机制。\n    - Ref: R90, R91\n\n    *Check against constraints:*\n    - One note per paper? Yes.\n    - Findings include methods, mechanisms, conditions? Yes.\n    - Quantitative results kept with metrics/subjects? Yes (HRs, n values, specific assays).\n    - Use_in_review specifies role? Yes.\n    - Explanation section: Needs to synthesize the author's explicit explanations of bidirectional regulation, receptors, and mechanisms without creating new cross-study summaries. Must be concrete.\n    - Remaining points: Briefly note unanswered questions from the text.\n\n    *Draft Explanation Section:*\n    文章明确指出，SCFAs、色氨酸衍生物和胆汁酸在不同肿瘤微环境及ICI靶点下呈现显著的双向调节作用，其方向取决于ICI类型、肿瘤组织学特征、代谢物空间分布（局部肠道vs全身循环/肿瘤组织）及宿主-微生物互作状态。\n    受体与信号机制方面：SCFAs主要通过激活G蛋白偶联受体（GPR41、GPR43、GPR109A）发挥免疫调节作用，其中GPR43激活可促进Treg功能并调控炎症小体；同时SCFAs作为组蛋白去乙酰化酶（HDAC）抑制剂，通过改变染色质结构上调Foxp3表达或增强CD8+ T细胞的代谢适应性（如解耦糖酵解与TCA循环）。在抗PD-1/PD-L1治疗中，SCFAs主要促进CD8+效应T细胞浸润与活化；而在抗CTLA-4治疗中，系统性SCFAs则倾向于扩张Treg细胞群，从而限制ICI抗肿瘤活性。\n    色氨酸代谢呈现“微生物促效-宿主抑效”的双向格局。微生物来源的吲哚类衍生物（如ICA、IPA、I-3-CA）主要作为芳烃受体（AHR）配体，激活AHR/IL-22轴或诱导I型干扰素（IFN-I）信号，进而促进CD8+ T细胞分化、减少Treg浸润并修复黏膜屏障。然而，宿主细胞高表达的IDO1酶会将色氨酸大量转化为犬尿氨酸，犬尿氨酸过度积累会直接导致T细胞功能障碍并诱发免疫抑制。因此，色氨酸代谢物的净效应取决于微生物吲哚合成能力与宿主IDO活性的相对平衡。\n    胆汁酸的作用高度依赖其化学结构、生成部位及受体亲和力。初级胆汁酸（如CDCA）可通过膜受体TGR5增强IFN-I表达以支持抗病毒/抗肿瘤免疫；而肠道菌群修饰产生的次级胆汁酸（如LCA、DCA）则表现出复杂的免疫抑制倾向。LCA及其衍生物可作为核受体FXR的强效配体，下调回肠血管内皮MAdCAM-1表达，破坏肠道对Treg17细胞的物理滞留，促使这些抑制性T细胞迁移至肿瘤微环境；DCA则通过抑制质膜Ca2+ ATPase阻断Ca2+-NFAT2信号传导，直接削弱CD8+ T细胞的效应功能。此外，胆汁酸在粪便（反映肠道局部代谢输出）与肝肿瘤组织（反映局部累积浓度）中的丰度变化常呈相反趋势，提示其空间药代动力学决定了最终是增强还是阻碍ICI疗效。\n    作者综合指出，这种双向性并非代谢物本身的固有矛盾，而是由“ICI靶点特异性（PD-1 vs CTLA-4）”、“肿瘤免疫微环境异质性”、“代谢物采样位点差异（粪便vs血清vs组织）”以及“抗生素暴露导致的菌群重塑”共同决定的上下文依赖（context-dependent）现象。\n\n    *Check remaining points:*\n    - Text mentions: \"The systemic impact of metabolites on distant cells and tissues remains largely unexplored.\" \"Factors such as the physicochemical properties... and host-specific characteristics... may further determine whether a metabolite acts locally or systemically. These factors warrant further study.\"\n    - \"Only inosine has been tested in a clinical trial... Other metabolites remain largely preclinical.\"\n    - \"Establishing a mechanistic understanding that links specific microbial strains or metabolites to immune functionality remains challenging. Causal relationships require validation using human-relevant systems...\"\n    - I will list these concisely.\n\n    *Final JSON Structure Check:*\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"question_material\": [\n        {\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"examples\": [ ... ],\n          \"explanation\": \"...\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [...]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n    ```\n    All constraints met. I will carefully format the JSON, ensuring proper escaping and st